WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.637
This is the Wanderer's Logbook.

00:00:02.637 --> 00:00:08.390
Every essay I have published since 2020, in English and Marathi, read as data.

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:12.791
A short prologue tells the story in dots:

00:00:12.791 --> 00:00:17.761
103 essays, the surge of 2026, two languages, and a map of meaning.

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:26.183
The Atlas places essays by what they say, so an English essay and a Marathi one about the same hills share a coast.

00:00:26.183 --> 00:00:28.812
Walk the route, in the order they were written.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:34.255
In the Sky, every first sentence becomes a constellation:

00:00:34.255 --> 00:00:35.731
one star for every word.

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:41.725
Take the words away, and each essay still has a fingerprint:

00:00:41.725 --> 00:00:43.845
its punctuation, spiralling out.

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:47.444
Phrases shows the habits of my hand.

00:00:47.444 --> 00:00:48.272
Then, a game:

00:00:48.272 --> 00:00:50.439
guess the year a line was written.

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:57.503
Letters pairs an old sentence with the new one closest to it in meaning, years apart.

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:02.002
Found poems cuts five essays into one poem.

00:01:02.002 --> 00:01:05.054
Lock the lines you love, and shuffle the rest.

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:12.060
And every essay opens as its own page, with its nearest neighbours, and a chat that knows it.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.455
The Wanderer's Logbook.

00:01:16.455 --> 00:01:18.957
At sankettambare.in/logbook.
